  "notes": "ぶつぶつ is an onomatopoeic word with two distinct meanings: (1) the sound of grumbling/muttering, and (2) a texture of small bumps, especially on skin.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS (muttering):\n- ぶつぶつ{言|い}う: to mutter, to grumble\n- ぶつぶつ{文句|もんく}を{言|い}う: to mutter complaints\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS (bumps):\n- ぶつぶつができる: bumps appear (on skin)\n- ぶつぶつが{出|で}る: bumps break out\n\nNOUN USAGE:\nWhen referring to skin bumps, ぶつぶつ functions as a noun: {肌|はだ}にぶつぶつが{出|で}た (bumps appeared on my skin). Casual alternative to {発疹|はっしん} (rash).\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ぼそぼそ: mumbling quietly (less complaining)\n- ぶつぶつ: implies dissatisfaction or complaint\n- つぶつぶ: grainy texture (small grains, not bumps)",
